1
00:00:01,720 --> 00:00:07,160
These three had elaborated Old Major's teachings into a complete system of thought,

2
00:00:07,160 --> 00:00:11,720
to which they gave the name of Animalism.

3
00:00:11,720 --> 00:00:16,319
Several nights a week, after Mr. Jones was asleep, they held secret meetings in

4
00:00:16,319 --> 00:00:21,160
the barn and expounded the principles of Animalism to the others.

5
00:00:21,160 --> 00:00:25,680
At the beginning, they met with much stupidity and apathy.

6
00:00:25,680 --> 00:00:31,640
Some of the animals talked of loyalty to Mr. Jones, whom they referred to as master,

7
00:00:31,640 --> 00:00:37,880
or made elementary remarks such as "Mr. Jones feeds us. If he were gone, we

8
00:00:37,880 --> 00:00:40,440
should starve to death."

9
00:00:40,440 --> 00:00:47,119
Others asked such questions as "Why should we care what happens after we are dead?"

10
00:00:47,119 --> 00:00:52,920
or "If this rebellion is to happen anyway, what difference does it make whether we

11
00:00:52,920 --> 00:00:55,319
work for it or not?"

12
00:00:55,319 --> 00:01:00,079
And the pigs had great difficulty in making them see that this was contrary

13
00:01:00,079 --> 00:01:03,200
to the spirit of animalism.

14
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:08,480
The stupidest questions of all were asked by Mollie, the white mare.

15
00:01:08,480 --> 00:01:14,119
The very first question she asked Snowball was >> "Will there still be sugar after the

16
00:01:14,119 --> 00:01:15,519
rebellion?"

17
00:01:15,519 --> 00:01:19,480
>> "No. We have no means of making sugar on this farm.

18
00:01:19,480 --> 00:01:22,160
Besides, you do not need sugar.

19
00:01:22,160 --> 00:01:25,640
You will have all the oats and hay you want."

20
00:01:25,640 --> 00:01:29,480
>> "And shall I still be allowed to wear ribbons in my mane?"

21
00:01:29,480 --> 00:01:36,400
>> "Comrade, those ribbons that you are so devoted to are the badge of slavery.

22
00:01:36,400 --> 00:01:41,519
Can you not understand that liberty is worth more than ribbons?"

23
00:01:41,519 --> 00:01:45,359
>> Mollie agreed, but she did not sound very convinced.

24
00:01:45,359 --> 00:01:53,000
The pigs had an even harder struggle to counteract the lies put about by Moses, the tame raven.

25
00:01:53,000 --> 00:02:00,400
Moses, who was Mr. Jones's especial pet, was a spy and a tale-bearer.

26
00:02:00,400 --> 00:02:03,720
But he was also a clever talker.

27
00:02:03,720 --> 00:02:10,519
He claimed to know of the existence of a mysterious country called Sugar Candy Mountain,

28
00:02:10,519 --> 00:02:14,519
to which all animals went when they died.

29
00:02:14,519 --> 00:02:21,240
It was situated somewhere up in the sky, a little distance beyond the clouds, Moses said.

30
00:02:21,240 --> 00:02:25,720
In Sugar Candy Mountain, it was Sunday 7 days a week.

31
00:02:25,720 --> 00:02:34,319
Clover was in season all the year round, and lump sugar and linseed cake grew on the hedges.

32
00:02:34,319 --> 00:02:40,640
The animals hated Moses because he told tales and did no work.

33
00:02:40,640 --> 00:02:44,079
But some of them believed in Sugar Candy Mountain.

34
00:02:44,079 --> 00:02:49,000
And the pigs had to argue very hard to persuade them that there was no such
